  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.04319v1</id>
    <title>AILS-NTUA at SemEval-2026 Task 12: Graph-Based Retrieval and Reflective Prompting for Abductive Event Reasoning</title>
    <updated>2026-03-04T17:38:52Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.04319v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2603.04319v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We present a winning three-stage system for SemEval 2026 Task~12: Abductive Event Reasoning that combines graph-based retrieval, LLM-driven abductive reasoning with prompt design optimized through reflective prompt evolution, and post-hoc consistency enforcement; our system ranks first on the evaluation-phase leaderboard with an accuracy score of 0.95. Cross-model error analysis across 14 models (7~families) reveals three shared inductive biases: causal chain incompleteness, proximate cause preference, and salience bias, whose cross-family convergence (51\% cause-count reduction) indicates systematic rather than model-specific failure modes in multi-label causal reasoning.</summary>
    <category term="cs.CL" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2026-03-04T17:38:52Z</published>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="cs.CL"/>
    <author>
